{"result":"{
  "id": "19144",
  "key": "SFCC-708",
  "summary": "PDP – Related Colours Attribute — BM / frontend",
  "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/issue/19144",
  "description": "As a Site Merchandiser, \nI want to manually link separate master products to each other using a Related Colours attribute in Business Manager, \nso that products with different style codes (which are not natural colour variants of the same master) can be associated and appear as selectable colour swatches on each other's PDP.\n\n----\n\nAdditional context: In Magento, merchandisers enter a comma-separated list of style codes (e.g. 9536JF261BLK,9536JF261CRM) into a field to establish these cross-product colour relationships. This replicates that capability in SFCC as a catalogue-level product attribute.\n\n\n\nin SFCC, BM, it will look like this: \n\n![\"image-20260812-060935.png\"](image-20260812-060935.png)",
  "status": {
    "name": "Ready for Development",
    "category": "To Do",
    "color": "blue-gray"
  },
  "issue_type": {
    "name": "Story"
  },
  "priority": {
    "name": "Medium"
  },
  "assignee": {
    "display_name": "Victor T. Crisostomo",
    "name": "Victor T. Crisostomo",
    "email": "victor.t.crisostomo@accenture.com",
    "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/557058:09af9e5b-661b-42a2-90ec-9ce9f69d324d/0ead87b0-7d31-4296-b27b-4a7b26ac2af1/48"
  },
  "reporter": {
    "display_name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
    "name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
    "email": "jasmijn.tsang@accenture.com",
    "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d/40fcd533-06f6-4e5b-ba9f-23879e1193f9/48"
  },
  "labels": [
    "Custom",
    "Squad-A"
  ],
  "created": "2026-08-12T14:55:41.994+1000",
  "updated": "2026-08-27T01:44:24.139+1000",
  "comments": [
    {
      "id": "13838",
      "body": "User:5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d This is approved, but wanted to flag the following: \n\n- If a related colour is added to a product but that related colour has not yet been enabled due to stock, then it shouldn’t appear as a swatch on the PDP until it is enabled. \n- When you are in the expanded Image Gallery view on the PDP there are swatches shown at the top of the gallery. The intended behaviour here is that the product images would change upon rollover of the swatch so the user can see the product quickly in different colours (not a full page load, they stay in the image gallery pop up).",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Dani Rivett",
        "name": "Dani Rivett",
        "email": null,
        "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/42d3d7910c25b8f4ba9e46aabfc6c149?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDR-3.png"
      },
      "created": "2026-08-13T12:31:07.716+1000",
      "updated": "2026-08-13T12:31:07.716+1000"
    },
    {
      "id": "13846",
      "body": "User:712020:4ec4770e-9470-4885-9753-69a36b6cf950 Hey Dani - had a chat with the team, here are my comments:\n- I have added an ac on this user story: \\*\\*Given a shopper is on the PDP, when the related colour product IDs are fetched and\\*\\* \\*\\*the product is not yet online (online flag is false, or current date is outside the online start and end date range)\\*\\*\\*\\*, then the swatch simply does not render on the PDP.\\*\nBy writing it this way, it’s not related to inventory but if you want - we can do the logic for inventory - but I was just thinking that if there’s no inventory but the product is coming soon / back in soon - wouldn’t we still want to show it so the customer can go to that PDP and sign up for notify me?\n- Unfortunately, the team mentioned we cannot meet that requirement in the expanded image gallery view because it would require a full page refresh as well - similar to how it is needed on the PDP itself after selecting that other colour swatch",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
        "name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
        "email": "jasmijn.tsang@accenture.com",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d/40fcd533-06f6-4e5b-ba9f-23879e1193f9/48"
      },
      "created": "2026-08-13T16:27:11.027+1000",
      "updated": "2026-08-13T16:27:11.027+1000"
    },
    {
      "id": "13856",
      "body": "User:5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d it should be based on whether the product is published on the frontend or not (not inventory). That way we can still promote Back In Soon/Coming Soon variations.\n\n\n\nIn regards to the colour swatch hover functionality, other sites do this without a full page refresh. Check out this Jacquemus example (which is where the design idea came from): [https://www.jacquemus.com/en*au/the-small-valerie/BAW00440AC09A04855.html](https://www.jacquemus.com/en*au/the-small-valerie/BAW00440AC09A04855.html)",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Dani Rivett",
        "name": "Dani Rivett",
        "email": null,
        "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/42d3d7910c25b8f4ba9e46aabfc6c149?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDR-3.png"
      },
      "created": "2026-08-13T17:43:27.441+1000",
      "updated": "2026-08-13T17:43:27.441+1000"
    },
    {
      "id": "13888",
      "body": "User:557058:09af9e5b-661b-42a2-90ec-9ce9f69d324d ready for your tech design review.",
      "author": {
        "display_name": "Hazel Marie Cacalda",
        "name": "Hazel Marie Cacalda",
        "email": "hazel.marie.i.banaz@accenture.com",
        "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/883ff1fae0c6179bdff495757469823d?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FHC-4.png"
      },
      "created": "2026-08-14T23:43:28.468+1000",
      "updated": "2026-08-14T23:43:28.468+1000"
    }
  ]
}"}

