{"result":"{
  "id": "18129",
  "key": "SFCC-91",
  "summary": "PDP UI — Colour Swatches & Variation Selection",
  "customfield_10231": {
    "value": "*Swatch availability*\n\n* Given a product has only one colour, when the PDP loads, then the colour is displayed as a text label (e.g. \"Colour: Bay Blue\") and no swatches are rendered.\n* Given a product has multiple colour variations, when the PDP loads, then the index image for each colour variation is displayed as a swatch.\n* Given multiple colour swatches are displayed, when the PDP loads, then the currently viewed colour variation's swatch is visually indicated as selected.\n\n*Swatch selection*\n\n* Colour variation: Given a shopper clicks a colour swatch, when the selection is registered, then the URL updates to reflect the selected colour variation without full page reload. \n\n*Index image not populated*\n\n* Given a colour variation exists but has not been enabled, when the PDP loads, then that colour variation's swatch is not rendered and the variation is not surfaced to the shopper."
  },
  "customfield_10232": {
    "value": "* This story has a hard dependency on the index image attribute being defined."
  },
  "customfield_10016": {
    "value": 3.0
  },
  "customfield_10015": {
    "value": null
  }
}"}

