  ],
  "customfield_10231": {
    "value": "1. Given a site merchandiser is editing a master product in Business Manager, when they navigate to the product's attributes, then a Related Colours attribute is available.\n2. Given the Related Colours attribute is visible, when the merchandiser enters one or more master product style codes, then the values are saved against that product.\n3. Given the field is populated, when the values are saved, then the order of style codes in the list determines the display order of colour swatches on the PDP.\n4. Given a style code entered in the field does not exist in the catalogue, when the attribute is saved, then no validation error is thrown at save time (the invalid entry is handled at render time).\n\n----\n\nFrom the front-end we still need to test this Acceptance Criteria then, copied from [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-91|https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-91|smart-link] :\n\nValid Related Product ID:\n5. Given a shopper clicks a colour swatch, when the selection is registered, then the URL updates to reflect the selected colour with a new style code and a full page reload.\n\nInvalid Related Product ID:\n6. Given a shopper is on the PDP, when the related colour product IDs are fetched and it's not a valid product ID, then the swatch simply does not render on the PDP.\n\nValid Related Product ID, product not yet online:\n\n7. Given a shopper is on the PDP, when the related colour product IDs are fetched and the product is not yet published (online flag is false, or current date is outside the online start and end date range), then the swatch simply does not render on the PDP."
  },
