    "value": "*Composition & layout*\n\n1. Given the component renders, then it displays the following elements in order from top to bottom as defined in the design system: product name + wishlist icon, price, product description, colour picker, size selector + Find your size link, add to bag CTA, Find in Boutique link, drawer trigger rows (Details & Care, Size Guide, Find My Size, Shipping & Returns, Assistance, & Environmental Qualities - EU only), model description, style code.\n2. Given the component renders on desktop, then layout and spacing between elements matches the design system spec.\n3. Given the component renders on mobile, then layout and spacing between elements matches the mobile design system spec.\n\n*Static content*\n\n4. Given the component renders, then product name, price, description, model description, and style code display in the typography styles defined in the design system.\n5. Given no product description is available, then the description element does not render and no empty space is left in its place.\n6. Given no model description is available, then the model description element does not render.\n7. Given no style code is available, then the style code element does not render.\n\n*Colour picker atom*\n\n8. Given the component renders, then the colour picker displays per the design system spec — refer to Figma for rendering states. Given only one colour variant exists, then no swatch row renders and only the \"Colour:\" label and colour name are displayed.\n\n*Size selector atom*\n\n9. Given the component renders, then the size selector displays per the design system spec — refer to Figma for all rendering states. The size selector must handle the following states passed in as props: default (no selection), filled (size selected), in-stock, low stock, out of stock, notify me, recommended, error, and one-size. Given the product is one-size, then the standard selector is suppressed and a plain \"One size\" label renders in its place and is treated as pre-selected.\n\n*Add to bag*\n\n10. Given no size has been selected, when a shopper activates the Add to Bag CTA, then a \"Size required\" inline message is displayed.\n11. Given a shopper selects an in-stock size, then the Add to Bag CTA is enabled.\n12. Given a shopper selects an out of stock size, then the Add to Bag CTA becomes disabled.\n\n*Drawer triggers*\n\n13. Given the component renders, then each drawer trigger row (Details & Care, Size & Fit, Find My Size, Shipping & Returns, Assistance) renders per the design system spec — refer to Figma for rendering and interaction states. Each trigger fires its respective drawer open event on activation; drawer content is out of scope for this story.\n\n*Find in Boutique link*\n\n14. Given the component renders, then the Find in Boutique link is visible below the Add to Bag CTA and fires the Find in Boutique panel trigger on click — the panel itself is out of scope for this story.\n\n*Accessibility*\n\n15. Given a keyboard user navigates through the component, then focus order follows the visual top-to-bottom reading order.\n16. The product name is marked up as a heading at the appropriate level in the page hierarchy.\n17. The component and all atoms meet WCAG 2.1 AA."
