    "content": {
      "value": "What we need to finalise user stories per epic\n----------------------------------------------\n\nPWA Kit user stories cannot be written, reviewed or signed off until the relevant design components are locked. Here is what that means in practice.\n\n### 1 — Components must be finalised first\n\n* Before user stories can be written for an epic e.g. Checkout Flow & Delivery, **every UI component that appears in that epic must be finalised in the UI kit** — fully componentised in Figma with all variations, states and responsive sizes accounted for. This allows us to build the component user story.\n* Each component is owned by the **earliest epic in the sequence where it appears**. That epic is responsible for designing all variations of that component — including any variations needed by later epics. For example, if a product card component appears on PDP, PLP and Homepage, all three variations must be designed and locked as part of the PDP.\n\n> As we move through the epic sequence, design effort should reduce. By the time we reach epics like Homepage or Wishlist, most components should already exist. Design at that stage should be limited to anything genuinely net-new.\n\n### 2 — Design freeze\n\n* **Hard rule:** Once a component is finalised and added to the UI kit, **it is locked — no further UX or design changes are permitted**. User stories are written against locked designs only. Any change after lock requires a formal review of every story and epic that references that component.\n\n### 3 — Sign-off checklist per epic\n\n* Before component user stories are submitted for PO review, confirm the component has ALL variations included in the UI kit.\n\n---\n\nComponent Design & User Story Tracker\n-------------------------------------\n\n| Epic | Example Design scope | Design components finalised | User stories ready for PO review | User stories ready for development | Design & user story sprint(s) | BA lead | Design lead |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| User mgmt & reporting – pt.1 | *No design required* | *Not required* | Aug 1 | Aug 8 | Sprint 2 | Jas | — |\n| PDP | PDP template, product card, size selector, ATC, recommendations carousel | Aug 13 (Sprint 3) | Aug 15 | Aug 24 | Sprint 2, Sprint 3 | Jas | Hannah |\n| Regional storefront | Country selector, language modal, currency indicator | Aug 24 (Sprint 3) | Aug 29 | Sep 7 | Sprint 2, Sprint 3, Sprint 4 | Jas |  |\n| Navigation | Nav bar, mega menu expanded state, mobile drawer, promotional banner | Aug 24 (Sprint 3) | Aug 29 | Sep 7 | Sprint 2, Sprint 3, Sprint 4 | Izzy |  |\n| Product catalogue | No design required | Not required | Aug 29 | Sep 7 | Sprint 2, Sprint 3, Sprint 4 | Jas | — |\n| Cart | Cart template, line items, order summary, promo code entry, empty state | Aug 24 (Sprint 3) | Aug 29 | Sep 7 | Sprint 2, Sprint 3, Sprint 4 | Izzy |  |\n| Search & recommendations | Search results page, predictive search overlay, recommended for you & recently viewed carousels | Aug 24 (Sprint 3) | Aug 29 | Sep 7 | Sprint 2, Sprint 3, Sprint 4 | Bianca |  |\n| Promotions | Promo/announcement bar, promotional badge on product card | Aug 24 (Sprint 3) | Aug 29 | Sep 7 | Sprint 3, Sprint 4 | Bianca |  |\n| PLP | PLP template, product grid, filter & sort panel, category header | Sep 7 (Sprint 4) | Sep 12 | Sep 21 | Sprint 2, Sprint 3, Sprint 4, Sprint 5 | Jas |  |\n| Pricing | *No design required* | *Not required* | Sep 12 | Sep 21 | Sprint 4, Sprint 5 | Jas | — |\n| Homepage | Homepage template, hero banner, editorial cards, featured category tiles | Sep 7 (Sprint 4) | Sep 12 | Sep 21 | Sprint 4, Sprint 5 | Izzy |  |\n| Checkout flow & delivery | Multi-step checkout template, delivery method selector, address form, order summary | Sep 7 (Sprint 4) | Sep 26 | Oct 5 | Sprint 5, Sprint 6 | Izzy |  |\n| Payments | Payment method selection, split payments, retail rewards redemption, order confirmation | Sep 7 (Sprint 4) | Sep 26 | Oct 5 | Sprint 5, Sprint 6 | Izzy |  |\n| Wishlist | Wishlist page in My Account, wishlist product card, empty state | Sep 21 (Sprint 5) | Sep 26 | Oct 5 | Sprint 5, Sprint 6 | Jas |  |\n| Returns & refunds | Returns flow in My Account, return method selection, refund status | Sep 21 (Sprint 5) | Sep 26 | Oct 5 | Sprint 6 | Jas |  |\n| Order management | Order confirmation page, My Orders list, order detail & tracking | Sep 21 (Sprint 5) | Sep 26 | Oct 5 | Sprint 6 | Jas |  |\n| Customer account & CRM | Login & registration, My Account dashboard, profile & preferences, saved addresses | Sep 21 (Sprint 5) | Sep 26 | Oct 5 | Sprint 5, Sprint 6 | Jas |  |\n| Store locator | Map & list view, store detail panel, search by location, opening hours | Sep 21 (Sprint 5) | Sep 26 | Oct 5 | Sprint 4, Sprint 5, Sprint 6 | Izzy |  |\n| Inventory | *No design required* | *Not required* | Oct 10 | Oct 19 | Sprint 7 | Izzy | — |\n| Credit notes & gift cards | Gift card entry, credit note display in account, redemption at checkout | Sep 21 (Sprint 5) | Oct 24 | Nov 2 | Sprint 7, Sprint 8 | Izzy |  |\n| ZIMMmerse | Immersive editorial template, rich media modules, shop-the-look | Sep 21 (Sprint 5) | Oct 24 | Nov 2 | Sprint 7, Sprint 8 | Izzy |  |\n| Client services (TBC) | Customer service chat widget (Scope TBC — SFCC or in-chat) | Sep 21 (Sprint 5) | Oct 24 | Nov 2 | Sprint 7, Sprint 8 | Izzy |  |\n| SEO, analytics & AB testing | *No design required* | *Not required* | — | Nov 2 | Sprint 7, Sprint 8 | — | — |\n| NFRs & observability | *No design required* | *Not required* | — | Nov 2 | Sprint 7, Sprint 8 | — | — |\n| User mgmt & reporting – pt.2 | *No design required* | *Not required* | Oct 24 | Nov 2 | Sprint 7, Sprint 8 | Jas | — |",
